# Home Lab Build — Proxmox, Wazuh SIEM, Pi-hole DNS
**Date:** June 30, 2026

## What I Did
- Migrated Proxmox node (HP ProDesk 400 G6) from 192.168.100.x to home network (10.0.0.50) by editing /etc/network/interfaces
- Built and installed Kali Linux VM (VM 100, 10.0.0.71) on Proxmox
- Built and installed Ubuntu Server VM (VM 101, 10.0.0.60) on Proxmox
- Built Windows Server 2022 VM (VM 103, 10.0.0.70) on Proxmox
- Deployed full Wazuh SIEM stack on Ubuntu Server using wazuh-install.sh — includes wazuh-manager, wazuh-indexer, wazuh-dashboard, and Filebeat
- Set static IPs on all VMs via netplan (Ubuntu) and SConfig (Windows Server)
- Installed Pi-hole on Raspberry Pi 3B+ at 10.0.0.100
- Changed Pi network config from dhcpcd to NetworkManager using nmcli
- Pointed personal-PC and lab VMs DNS to Pi-hole (10.0.0.100)
- Set router DHCP range to 10.0.0.151-254 to reserve 10.0.0.50-150 for static lab devices
- Enabled RDP on Windows Server via SConfig

